            "review_text": "Yasu | Matsumoto Castle Guide\nJapan110 contributions\n0\nThere are local customers, but many are foreigners\nMar 2026 • Solo\nTwo-thirds of the visitors are foreigners and about one-third are local. It was very crowded and I shared a seat with another local guest. I asked for phở bò kho (beef stew pho), which was recommended by word of mouth. This is beef stewy and delicious, but the classic light pho may still be my favorite. I didn't think the price was so low at VND 84,000. Finally, I paid in cash, but when I looked at the receipt, it said Khăn Lạnh 2,000 dong (about $12) in addition to Pho, and when I looked it up in the dictionary, it said \"cold towel = oshibori.\" I did use the disposable oshibori that was on the table.\nRead more\nTranslated from Japanese\nShow original\nWritten March 22, 2026",
